        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/n/91b2a8/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2018-04-29T20:18:40.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I ran the first issue of the Sentinels RPG last night and I had a question.&nbsp; How does spatial stuff work?&nbsp; Like, what counts as close for Ab Zero's mass hinder?&nbsp; What constitutes a group for the purposes of Legacy's flying smash?&nbsp; How does Tachyon's principle of speed work?&nbsp; And how do Tachyon's hypersonic assault and sonic vortex abilities work?&nbsp; My players were getting completely overwhelmed by bots in the final battle of the first issue, since they had a run of bad rolls against the mothership, which resulted in me having to fudge the fight, with some of the robots just leaving mid-fight to join the harvesters and groups assembling into threes like the previous fight.&nbsp; It just wasn't super fun for them and I want to know how to manipulate space better so that the players either will or won't get run over by the enemies.&nbsp;</p>",
        "post_number": 1,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:51:13.547Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
